-- title:
--   Address ordering in the encoded-color pipeline
-- statement:
--   Let $f,n\in\mathbb N$ and let $A,B,C$ be strictly increasing integer lists. Use the pipeline's derived addresses: $p$ for the prime header, $c$ for the cover base, $w$ for the wanted header, $q$ for the source controls, $b$ for the bank header, and $e$ for the finishing address. The wanted header uses the length of the normalized incidence list; all other parameters are those determined by $n,A,B,C$. Then
--
--   $$
--   p+6\le c,\quad f+8\le c,\quad c\le q,\quad w+4\le q,\quad q+3\le e,\quad b+5\le e.
--   $$
--
--   These exact inequalities place the relevant header extents before the later allocations, supplying the memory-preservation bounds needed to compose the pipeline stages.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorPipelineData.lean#L82-L107

